# Chaos: typed impact numbers (client/BASE.md 0100; server src-patch 0051; after 0001-0083, numbered 0100 to leave room
# for the patches in flight). Login: bit 7 of the capability byte asks the server for typed numbers; the server answers
# with feature GameChaosImpactText (155), which is cleared before every login, so an older server keeps the old layout.
# With it, every damage, heal, mana and experience text message carries u16 percent (x100), u8 type (0 normal,
# 1 critical, 2 condition tick, 3 mana drain, 4 mana gain, 5 energy shield, 6+ scripts) and u32 creature id after its
# value / colour pairs, before the text. Each number goes through the Lua hook
# g_map.onImpactText(animatedText, text, mode, typeId, value, percent, creatureId, pos) before it reaches the map
# (true drops it; called with type 0 against an older server too). AnimatedText: a drift that replaces the stock rise
# (setAnimationSpeed {x, y}: pixels over the whole life), setFadeStart, setStackWithOtherTexts (false: no merge, no
# side-by-side layout), the impact type / value / percent, setText / setColor / setFont for Lua, and a weak pointer to
# the creature it belongs to; removal at the text's own life. merge() also needs the same type, creature and stacking.
# GameChaosAttachedImpactText (156, client only): MapView draws an attached number at its creature's tile moved by the
# creature's walk and jump, so it follows the creature while it floats; a removed, hidden or other-floor creature
# leaves it where the creature was last seen (its own tile if never seen). Options > Interface "Damage numbers follow
# the creature" (`attachedImpactText`, on); the overlay module game_damagescatter applies it at every game start.
